<?nvs
// A child isolate of `examples/isolate.nvs` that fails. ADR 0006 §
// *Failure is a value, not an exception*: this throw does not cross the
// boundary as a throw. The parent's `await` answers with a `ScriptResult`
// whose `ok` is false and whose `error` carries the message — which is what
// keeps a child's failure from being able to end the parent.
throw new RuntimeError('child could not finish');
